site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":20,"created_at":"2026-01-29T06:44:17Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T11:54:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.6.stable\n- Not reproducible in Godot 4.5.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 4 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8157) - AMD Ryzen 5 2600 Six-Core Processor (12 threads) - 15.94 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI have now upgraded 2 projects from Godot 4.5.1 to Godot 4.6. When I export the web versions and upload them to itch, I now get Memory Access Out of Bounds errors. The only thing that changed was the Godot version.\n\n<img width=\"641\" height=\"358\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d18150cf-185e-4d02-8e9b-860ea9399d58\" />\n\nThis is what the Chrome Debugger has to say about it with a debug build:\n\n<img width=\"549\" height=\"627\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/27fd4630-6a50-4f1a-ab72-74992659c641\" />\n\nEven weirder, when I created a brand new Godot 4.6 project and uploaded it, I had no problems.\n\nFor now, I’ve reverted back to 4.5. Doing so allowed me to export a working Web project.\n\nGodot Forums Thread: https://forum.godotengine.org/t/memory-access-out-of-bounds-on-web-export-migrating-4-5-1-4-6/131968/2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Updated two projects from Godot 4.5.1.stable to Godot 4.6.stable, with no other changes.\n2. Did Web Exports on both and replaced the existing web exports on itch.io.\n\n**RESULT:** Both exports failed due to \"memory access out of bounds\" error (_see screen shot above_).\n**EXPECTED:** The games would load as normal.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThis is the smaller (and open source/public) project I had the problem with:\nhttps://github.com/dragonforge-dev/dragonforge-sound/releases\n\nYou can either use the v0.16 release for Dragonforge Sound, or grab the v0.15 release and upgrade it. Obviously you'll have to have an itch account to post it to.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115560/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115560/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}